From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patryk Kowalczyk <papyszoo@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 01:04:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: the hot BetterVR hooks stop copying actors and strings,
 and say what they cost

hook_RouteActorJob reads the actor name in place and compares the job string directly instead of copying ActorWiiU (0x538 bytes) and building two std::strings per actor job. hook_ModifyBoneMatrix compares the model name without a std::string per bone and keeps the bone name as a string_view, with heterogeneous map lookups. hook_CheckIfCameraCanSeePos reads the XR views and the gameplay base pose once per call instead of once per eye, and hook_SetActorOpacity reads only the opacity field. IsTrackedPlayerBody reads the three player fields instead of copying PlayerBase (0x12A8 bytes) per rigid body setter, whose ROOMSCALE logging now returns before reading when the category is off. Every 64th call of the five hottest hooks is timed and the [diag] line prints their host time as ms/s and calls per game frame.
